    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "As the error message says, `write()` needs a name of the session in order to name the file accordingly. Using plain `MiniSessions.write()` is possible only if there is already read session, which there is not.\r\nTry something like `lua MiniSessions.write('my-session')`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">As the error message says, <code class=\"notranslate\">write()</code> needs a name of the session in order to name the file accordingly. Using plain <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniSessions.write()</code> is possible only if there is already read session, which there is not.<br>\nTry something like <code class=\"notranslate\">lua MiniSessions.write('my-session')</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "As the error message says, write() needs a name of the session in order to name the file accordingly. Using plain MiniSessions.write() is possible only if there is already read session, which there is not.\nTry something like lua MiniSessions.write('my-session').",
